  m_Name: AncientEldonData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcData
  npcID: ancient_eldon
  displayName: Ancient Eldon
  description: The wisest elder of Cardland and the head of Leymar. Eldon remembers old paths, forgotten rules, and the price of every careless choice.
  disposition: 1
  maxHealth: 30
  startingArmor: 0
  worldSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e31786befe2e14e4993fb0aa337d7777, type: 3}
  dialogueSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b70460a0a86efc14ba06691c92c47257, type: 3}
  dialogueLines:
  - Welcome, traveler. Few reach Leymar by accident, and fewer still leave unchanged.
  - Cardland remembers every hand that was played. Listen closely, and you may hear what the cards refuse to say.
  - The Screen is not only a border. It is a wound between what is seen and what is hidden.
  - If you seek answers, begin with patience. If you seek power, begin with restraint.
  overheadLines:
  - The old screen hums again.
  - Leymar is listening.
  - Every card has a memory.
  questIDs: []
  tradeStock: []
  canMove: 0
  moveSpeed: 2
